    "title": "<p>Summary of lipomatosis phenotypes</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Jennifer Olivia Black",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"926\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Lipomatosis subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Location</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Age</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Distinguishing features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Genes involved</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>CILF</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Face</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Congenital</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unilateral; overgrowth of adjacent tissues</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>PIK3CA</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">DL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Trunk, extremities</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;years</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Large, segmental, rapidly growing mass; associated with tuberous sclerosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Not known</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>ECCL</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Head</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Congenital</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Naevus psiloliparus; CNS malformations and tumours; ocular abnormalities; developmental delay; seizures</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>FGFR1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">MTBS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Generalized</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Congenital</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Excess skin folds; dysmorphic facial features; genitourinary abnormalities; smooth muscle hamartomas; developmental delay</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">No consistent abnormality</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>PHOST</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Extremities, rarely trunk and face</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;15&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Painful infiltrative intramuscular hamartomatous lesion with fat, vascular malformation, and other mesenchymal elements; Cowden syndrome; Bannayan&ndash;Riley&ndash;Ruvalcaba syndrome</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>PTEN</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">PROS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Extremities</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Congenital, early childhood</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Progressive disproportionate asymmetrical mesenchymal overgrowth lesions with a variety of clinical constellations: polydactyly, syndactyly, macrocephaly, urinary tract abnormalities, LN, FAO, CLOVES, MCAP, HHML, FAVA</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">PIK3CA</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>FML</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Extremities, trunk, viscera, head and neck</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">30&ndash;40&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Onset in middle age; sometimes multiple; autosomal dominant inheritance; increased cancer risk</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>HMGA2</em>, <em>PALB2</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 78.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">MSL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Neck, shoulders, trunk</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Middle age</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 324.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"433\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Adult onset in men with chronic alcoholism</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.45pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"134\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">MT-TK</span></em><span style=\"color: black;\"> (<em>MERRF</em>), mitochondrial genes, <em>MFN2</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CILF, congenital infiltrating lipomatosis of the face; CLOVES, CLOVES syndrome (congenital lipomatous overgrowth, vascular malformations, epidermal naevi, and scoliosis or skeletal/spinal anomalies); DL, diffuse lipomatosis; ECCL, encephalocraniocutaneous lipomatosis; FAO, fibroadipose overgrowth; FAVA, fibroadipose vascular anomaly; FML, familial multiple lipomatosis; HHML, hemihyperplasia&ndash;multiple lipomatosis syndrome; LN, lipomatosis of nerve; MCAP, megalencephaly&ndash;capillary malformation syndrome; MSL, multiple symmetrical lipomatosis; MTBS, Michelin tire baby syndrome; PHOST, <em>PTEN</em> hamartoma of soft tissue; PROS, <em>PIK3CA</em>-related overgrowth spectrum.</p>",
